to understand what factors of  polynomials are and how they can be used  we need to understand the basics of  factorization first we start with simple  numbers how do we find the factors of  the number six to find the factors of  six ask yourself how can we write 6 as a  product of two numbers we can write 6 as  one multiplied by 6 and also 2  multiplied by 3 is there any other  combination you can think of no there  isn't any so the factors of 6 are these  four numbers 1 2 3 &amp; 6 1 is a factor of  6 since there is some natural number  that it can be multiplied with to get  the original number similarly 2 3 &amp; 6  are also factors but the number four is  not a factor of 6 because it cannot be  multiplied with a natural number to get  a 6 let us also try finding factors for  the number 8 8 can be written as 1  multiplied by 8 and 2 x 4 there is no  other combination of the two numbers  which gives us 8 so the factors of 8 are  1 2 4 &amp; 8 this can also be seen in a  different way if we divide a number by  any of its factors the remainder will  always be 0 if you divide 6 by 3 you  will get 2 as the quotient if you divide  6 by 1 you will get 6 as the quotient if  you divide 8 by 2 you will get 4 as the  quotient in all the cases the remainder  is 0 how does this help us what if we  want to know whether a number is a  factor of another number or not for  example if we want to know whether it is  a factor of 216 what would you do this  is where division helps us if you want  to know whether 8  is a factor of 216 all we need to do is  divide 216 by 8 after the division if we  get the remainder as 0 we can say that 8  is a factor of 216 so let us divide 216  by 8 yes the traditional way where we  write 216 like this and 8 next to it  after solving we get the quotient as 27  and the remainder as 0 as the remainder  is 0 we can say that 8 is a factor of  216 we can write 216 as 8 multiplied by  27 what else can we say after looking at  this process is 27 a factor of 216 yes  as we can write 216 as 8 x 27 27 is also  a factor of 216 remember 8 and 27 are  two of the many factors of 216 this  division just helps us to know if 8 is a  factor of 216 or not and if we find out  that the divisor is a factor then the  quotient as well has to be a factor  let's see if 9 is a factor of 216 we  will have to divide two hundred and  sixteen by nine so after we finish our  division process we see that the  remainder is zero so 9 is a factor of  216 and since 216 can also be written as  9 x 24 24 is also a factor of 216 in the  process of finding out if 8 and 9 are  factors of 216 we also found out two  more factors of 216 27 and 24 what about  10 is it a factor of 216 to find out we  divide 216 by 10  in this case we get the remainder as six  as it's not zero we can say that 10 is  not a factor of 216 we can also conclude  that 21 is not a factor of 216 remember  if the remainder is zero the divisor and  the quotient are both factors of the  dividend  you
 

